**Option 2: Create a placeholder SVG that can be converted to PNG**

```typescript
// scripts/generate-placeholder-banner.ts
import { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'fs';
import { join } from 'path';

/**
 * Generates a placeholder banner SVG for member benefits
 * This should be replaced with actual design assets from the design team
 */
const generatePlaceholderBanner = (): void => {
  const width = 1200;
  const height = 300;
  
  const svgContent = `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<svg width="${width}" height="${height}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="grad" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
      <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color:#4F46E5;stop-opacity:1" />
      <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color:#7C3AED;stop-opacity:1" />
    </linearGradient>
  </defs>
  <rect width="${width}" height="${height}" fill="url(#grad)"/>
  <text x="50%" y="40%" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="48" font-weight="bold" fill="white" text-anchor="middle">
    Member Benefits
  </text>
  <text x="50%" y="60%" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="24" fill="white" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.9">
    Placeholder - Design Asset Needed
  </text>
  <text x="50%" y="75%" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" fill="white" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.7">
    ${width}x${height}px
  </text>
</svg>`;

  const outputDir = join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'assets', 'images');
  mkdirSync(outputDir, { recursive: true });
  
  const outputPath = join(outputDir, 'member-benefits-banner.svg');
  writeFileSync(outputPath, svgContent, 'utf-8');
  
  console.log(`✓ Placeholder banner generated at: ${outputPath}`);
  console.log('⚠ This is a placeholder. Replace with actual design asset from design team.');
};

generatePlaceholderBanner();
```

**Action Required:**

Since this is a binary PNG image file, you need to:

1. Contact the design team to provide the actual banner image
2. Place the received PNG file at: `public/assets/images/member-benefits-banner.png`
3. Recommended specifications:
   - Width: 1200-1920px
   - Height: 200-400px
   - Format: PNG with transparency support
   - File size: < 500KB (optimized)
   - Resolution: @2x for retina displays

For now, create an empty `.gitkeep` file or use the TypeScript script above to generate a placeholder SVG until the design asset is provided.